Love the focus on hidden gems! For dataset cards, what really makes them useful is *actionable transparency*. A great card doesn’t just list sources and size—it clearly documents biases, data collection methods, and real-world use cases (and limitations!). I’ve found that including a simple datasheet with licensing, update frequency, and example use cases (like “Not suitable for medical diagnosis”) saves hours of trial and error. Bonus points if it’s versioned alongside the dataset!  

